Stream of steps with functions -> Functional programming

Why Stream?
    - Multiple data sources, so convert to stream to make all usable in same way
    - Intermediate operations (filter, map, etc)
    - Terminal Operations (forEach(), collect(), reduce())
        - Intermediate Operations wait for a terminal operation
    - More efficient, optimized for performance, can leverage parallelism
    - Enable declarative, readable and efficient data processing

Core principles
    - Functions as first-class citizens
    - Immutability, prefer and avoid changing state
    - Should not modify external state, pure functions

Lambda Functions
    - Method without a name
        - (Parameters) -> expression
        - (Parameters) -> { statements;}
        - can Type declare (int x) -> x + 10

    - Functional interface, an interface with a single abstract method
    - Lambda Expression, provides the implementation
    - Runtime, Lambda is converted to an instance of the functional interface
    - Execution


Intermediate Operations are executed only when a terminal operation is invoked


Mapping data with streams
    - map()
    - flatMap(), for nested collections or expanding data


Reduce()
    - Combine elements of a stream into a single result using an identity value and an associative accumulation function



